## Transaction and storage dependencies

The PostgreSQL adapter needs an existing dataset Service, selected transaction
Store, private dataset Store namespace, configured draft processor and typed
policy. SourceImporter streams input and normalizes under bounded source,
output, row and deadline policies. Parquet additionally requires an admitted,
hash-locked offline PyArrow interpreter. The existing JSONL draft path remains.

Use authenticated server tenant/workspace and current membership/delegated
authority. Lock the selected local dataset before any upload-body read; take
site/cell from local_site_id()/local_cell_id(), and receipt scope from the
exact local draft. Refuse foreign drafts before replay/body reads. Recheck
authority and capacity in the final owner transaction. Draft, inspection job,
receipt and audit commit together in that transaction. Private original and
normalized bytes are verified and synced before the SQL reference commits.
On a lost commit acknowledgement preserve that attempt's files and reconcile
with the same idempotency key; do not report success from an unknown commit.
No sidecar database owns the authoritative report.

Read/replay requires current authorization and matching six-field scope, then
verifies both original and normalized counts and SHA-256 against the persisted
report and draft. The report endpoint and upload composition are opt-in module
fixtures, not production routes. Installed runtime grants, coordinated release
catalog and public API composition remain shared-owner integration work.

